# Rahadin, the count's chamberlain (docs/voice/rahadin.md; docs/regions/castle_ravenloft_court.md).
# start: the first meeting in the King's Hall (approach). chamber: in his room on the floor above.
# intercept: at the head of the grand stairs when the party leaves with Gertruda.

~ start
if flag.rahadin_met
Rahadin: You are still here. Good. The master dislikes guests who leave early.
-> menu
endif
set rahadin_met
Narrator: A small, straight-backed man in black waits in the middle of the long hall with his hands folded. Around him, faint as a draught under a door, many voices are screaming.
Rahadin: You came up the grand stair, so you are the master's guests. I am Rahadin. I keep this house.
Rahadin: There are three rules. Go where you like. Take nothing that is not offered. Do not touch the girl.
interject class:cleric: Those voices. They're coming from you.
Rahadin: They are mine. I have collected them for a long time. You need not listen.
-> menu

~ chamber
if not flag.rahadin_met
set rahadin_met
Narrator: A bare room: a cot, a rack of curved swords, a ledger on a stand. A small man in black sits on the cot polishing a blade, and the air around him is full of faint screaming.
Rahadin: You found my room before you found me. Most guests manage it the other way round. I am Rahadin. I keep this house.
else
Narrator: Rahadin looks up from his blade. The screaming in the room rises a little, as if to see who has come.
Rahadin: Guests do not usually come this far along the corridor. Those who do, I remember.
endif
-> menu

~ menu
* Where is your master? -> master
* What girl? -> girl
* What are those voices? -> voices
* How long have you served him? -> service
* [Insight DC 15] What does he really want from us? -> insight_ok | insight_fail
* [if guest:ireena] You know who this is. -> ireena
* [name:wren_featherfoot] [if quest.the_last_lesson >= the_brother and not flag.wren_rahadin_met] Tell him who your teacher was. -> companions/lesson:rahadin
* We didn't come as guests. -> fight
* We'll find our own way. -> leave

~ master
Rahadin: In the house. He is always in the house, even when he is not. He receives when he chooses.
if tarokka.drawn
Rahadin: If an old woman has turned cards for you, you know more than I am permitted to say. Her cards are seldom wrong. It annoys him.
endif
-> menu

~ girl
Rahadin: A guest of the master, in the rooms above. She is content. Leave her so.
if flag.gertruda_search_promised
interject tag:blunt: Dark-haired girl? Sixteen? From the village?
Rahadin: I do not ask their ages.
endif
-> menu

~ voices
Rahadin: Everyone I have killed in his service. They do not leave me. It is the price of a long career, and I pay it.
interject class:wizard: That isn't a curse. He keeps them on purpose.
Rahadin: I keep accounts. Lipsiege keeps the master's money. I keep the rest.
-> menu

~ service
Rahadin: Since before this valley had his name. I served the man; I serve what he became. The house needs keeping either way.
interject species:elf: You're elven. Or you were. What are you now?
Rahadin: Punctual.
-> menu

~ insight_ok
Narrator: Under the courtesy he is weighing you, the way a steward weighs candles: how long you will burn, and what you will cost.
Rahadin: He wants to be amused. Amuse him, and you will live longer than most.
-> menu

~ insight_fail
Narrator: His face gives you nothing at all. It has had centuries of practice.
-> menu

~ ireena
Rahadin: I know the face. Everyone in this house knows the face. Her rooms have been ready for a very long time.
interject guest:ireena: Then they can stay empty.
-> menu

~ fight
Rahadin: As you wish. He will want to hear how it went.
if at:castle_ravenloft_court_weeping
combat court_rahadin_chamber_fight
else
combat court_rahadin_fight
endif

~ leave
Rahadin: Then I will not keep you. Supper is at dusk, if the master remembers to serve it.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Leaving with Gertruda

~ intercept
if not flag.rahadin_met
set rahadin_met
Narrator: A small man in black stands at the head of the grand stairs with his hands folded, and the air around him is full of faint screaming.
Rahadin: I am Rahadin. I keep this house, and I keep its guests.
endif
Narrator: Rahadin stands between you and the stairs. He looks past you at Gertruda, and she steps behind the nearest of you.
Rahadin: The girl is the master's guest. She stays.
if flag.court_gertruda_warned_him
Rahadin: She rang for him an hour ago and told him what you said. He asked me to see her safely back upstairs. I always do what he asks.
endif
Gertruda [afraid]: I want to go home. I'm allowed to want that. Aren't I?
-> intercept_menu

~ intercept_menu
* Then we go through you. -> fight
* [if not flag.court_gertruda_warned_him] [Persuasion DC 16] A guest who can't leave is a prisoner. Does your master keep prisoners in his guest rooms? -> stand_aside | refused
* [Intimidation DC 17] Look at us, Rahadin. You're one man. -> stand_aside | refused
* Gertruda, go back to your room. -> give_back

~ stand_aside
set rahadin_stood_aside
Narrator: For a long moment the only sound is the screaming. Then Rahadin steps aside, exactly one pace.
Rahadin: The master will be amused. She will come back on her own; they generally do. Mind the stairs.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +2 thistle +1 kip_smudgewick +1: You made Rahadin stand aside for Gertruda
-> END

~ refused
Rahadin: No. I think not.
combat court_rahadin_fight

~ give_back
leave gertruda
set gertruda_given_back
quest find_gertruda lost
Gertruda [sad]: Oh. Yes. Of course. I'll go up.
Narrator: She climbs the stairs alone and doesn't look back. Rahadin bows to you, very correctly.
Rahadin: The master thanks you for returning what is his.
approve godrick_pendlebrook -5 kip_smudgewick -4 liriel_dawnsong -3 thistle -3 wren_featherfoot -3 ratatoille -2: You sent Gertruda back up the stairs to Strahd
-> END
